\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.1}{\ignorespaces Standard IID Evaluation ($\alpha =1000$): RoLoRA vs.\ FDA-RoLoRA across GLUE benchmarks.}}{39}{table.5.1}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.2}{\ignorespaces Non-IID Evaluation ($\alpha =0.5$): RoLoRA vs.\ FDA-RoLoRA across GLUE benchmarks under Dirichlet label skew.}}{40}{table.5.2}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.3}{\ignorespaces Detailed Telemetry Across All IID Configurations ($\alpha =1000$): Comprehensive multi-seed final/peak accuracy, executed communication rounds, exact communication cost (accounting for 3-layer SST-2 structure), realized local epochs, and inter-client drift variance.}}{41}{table.5.3}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.4}{\ignorespaces Detailed Telemetry Across All Non-IID Configurations ($\alpha =0.5$): Performance under Dirichlet distribution skew. The corrupted 4-round MNLI $C=20$ $k=1.0$ run has been removed, demonstrating true multi-seed stability ($72.87 \pm 0.94\%$ final accuracy). Factor-decomposed local epochs $\bar {e}_A$ and $\bar {e}_B$ show symmetric tracking across alternating tracks.}}{52}{table.5.4}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.5}{\ignorespaces Convergence Milestone Efficiency: Communication rounds and cumulative payload required to surpass predefined target accuracy milestones. Milestones are selected a priori above majority-class baselines. Individual seed trajectories are tracked to prevent averaging artifacts.}}{57}{table.5.5}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.6}{\ignorespaces Matched-Budget Communication Parity: Validation accuracy evaluated strictly at identical communication payload budgets (Common Budget MB) and identical round horizons across RoLoRA and FDA-RoLoRA.}}{58}{table.5.6}%
\contentsline {table}{\numberline {5.7}{\ignorespaces Empirical Closed-Loop Controller Setpoint Tracking: Comparison of nominal targets $k \cdot e_{\max }$ against realized steady-state local epochs $\bar {e}_{\text {ss}}$ and tracking ratio $\mathcal {S} = \bar {e}_{\text {ss}} / (k \cdot e_{\max })$. In IID regimes, super-linear client variance growth causes steady-state undershoot ($\mathcal {S} \approx 0.64\text {--}0.79$); in Non-IID regimes, near-linear variance allows near-optimal setpoint tracking ($\mathcal {S} \approx 0.91\text {--}1.11$). Realized epochs for matrices $A$ and $B$ confirm track symmetry.}}{58}{table.5.7}%
